Krita Nova 41 - faster filter and adjustment previews

The preview of the filter dialog (Filter > ..., Adjust > ...) filters only
the visible part of the canvas while you change the settings:

- The part is the canvas' region of interest: the visible area plus a
  margin of a quarter of it on each side. Panning or zooming so that an
  unfiltered part becomes visible previews again; OK filters the whole layer
  (and the other selected frames, if enabled).
- Only for filters that work in patches (supportsThreading()): those give
  the same result for any split of the layer, so the visible part looks
  exactly like the final result. The others, and wrap-around mode, still
  preview everything. Zoomed out, the preview keeps using the lower level of
  detail as before.
- KisFilterStrokeStrategy::setPreviewRect(), KisFilterManager::apply(config,
  previewRect) / isPartialPreview(), KisDlgFilter::previewArea().

Color adjustments (Hue/Saturation, Levels, Curves, Brightness/Contrast,
Color Balance, Desaturate, Posterize, ... - every KisColorTransformationFilter,
also in filter masks and adjustment layers) transform a run of four or more
equal pixels once and copy the result: transparent areas and flat colors
cost almost nothing now.
